or you're too far gone, the cross cries a different answer.

354
00:45:41,000 --> 00:45:48,000
For God so loved you that He gave His one and only Son.

355
00:45:48,000 --> 00:45:54,000
And then the other side of that, people rejecting God's forgiveness, not receiving God's forgiveness.

356
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:57,000
This, I think, is becoming more prevalent in our culture, and that's, we just don't think we're that bad.

357
00:45:57,000 --> 00:46:00,000
We think we're pretty good.

358
00:46:03,000 --> 00:46:06,000
I can't, I don't deserve God's wrath. Other people might.

359
00:46:06,000 --> 00:46:20,000
And so, if that's you, I would just ask you to sit with some of your worst days.

360
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:26,000
I ask you to think about some of the worst decisions you've made and some of the ways that that has negatively impacted people.

361
00:46:31,000 --> 00:46:36,000
And some of those actions that we've perpetuated are going to negatively impact people for the rest of their lives.

362
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:43,000
And we've justified it and pushed it into the darkness. And we're good moving forward. We're pretty good people.

363
00:46:43,000 --> 00:46:53,000
I think the cross of Jesus reminds us that even the smallest of sins that we justify away is worthy of God's wrath.

364
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:59,000
And if we haven't received the forgiveness of Jesus on the cross through the cup of the covenant in his blood,

365
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:04,000
a day will come when his wrath will be poured out.

366
00:47:04,000 --> 00:47:09,000
And my invitation to you is don't let that day come for you.

367
00:47:09,000 --> 00:47:13,000
That day could have already came for you 2,000 years ago on the cross.

368
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:16,000
Will you receive that forgiveness and that grace?

369
00:47:16,000 --> 00:47:21,000
And I think for those of us that have already trusted in Christ, believers,

370
00:47:21,000 --> 00:47:27,000
our response is to joyfully receive this cup with sober gladness

371
00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:34,000
and join with the saints in Revelation who declare standing on top victoriously of the chaos waters.

372
00:47:34,000 --> 00:47:38,000
Great and amazing are your deeds, O Lord, God Almighty.

373
00:47:38,000 --> 00:47:41,000
Just and true are your ways, O King of the nations.

374
00:47:41,000 --> 00:47:45,000
Who will not fear, O Lord, and glorify your name? For you alone are holy.

375
00:47:45,000 --> 00:47:53,000
All the nations will come and worship you, for your righteous acts have been revealed in Jesus.

376
00:47:57,000 --> 00:48:03,000
God's wrath is good because he is good. It is most clearly demonstrated in the person and work of Jesus.

377
00:48:03,000 --> 00:48:09,000
God desires repentance and not rejection. He is patient, but that patience will come to an end.

378
00:48:09,000 --> 00:48:12,000
Today, if you hear his voice, do not harden your heart.

379
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:15,000
So as we take communion...
